@startuml signal-correlation
title US-06: Signal Correlation - Two Weak Signals Joined via Neo4j

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j

note over Evaluator
  Runs on each evaluation cycle.
  Only the elected leader emits alerts.
end note

Evaluator -> Redis : check entity:live:{entity_b} TTL
Redis --> Evaluator : key missing - Entity B is dark

note over Evaluator
  Weak signal 1: signal loss detected.
  Not actionable on its own.
end note

Evaluator -> Neo4j : MATCH (b:Entity {id: $id_b})-[e:PROXIMITY_EVENT]->(a:Entity)\nWHERE e.timestamp_ms > $dark_since_ms\nAND NOT (b)-[:KNOWN_ASSOCIATE]-(a)\nRETURN a, e

note over Neo4j
  Multi-hop graph traversal:
  find all entities that came near
  Entity B after it went dark,
  with no prior KNOWN_ASSOCIATE edge.
  Single Cypher pattern match.
end note

Neo4j --> Evaluator : Entity A, proximity event { lat, lon, timestamp_ms, distance_metres }

note over Evaluator
  Weak signal 2: proximity to unrelated entity
  within the signal loss window.
  Together they form a composite pattern.
end note

Evaluator -> Evaluator : correlate signals\n-> COMPOSITE alert at elevated priority

@enduml
